---
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Playground: build and copy a snippet" description="Pick an iVOLT component, a variant, a size and a panel theme, see it rendered live, then copy the HTML straight into your page. No account, no build step.">
  <article class="docs-prose">
    <h1>Playground</h1>
    <p>
      This is a <strong>snippet generator</strong>, not an editor. You choose a component, a
      variant, a size where it applies, a theme for the preview panel and one of a few sample
      strings; the page builds the markup from fixed templates and shows you the HTML to copy.
      There is no free-form input and no code is executed, so what you copy is always valid
      iVOLT markup. Nothing is stored: reload the page and you are back to the defaults.
    </p>
    <p class="docs-meta"><strong>Runs:</strong> in this page, from fixed templates. <strong>Stores:</strong> nothing. <strong>Executes:</strong> no code you type — there is nothing to type.</p>
    <noscript>
      <div class="iv-alert iv-alert--info" role="status">
        <p class="iv-alert__title">The playground needs JavaScript</p>
        <div class="iv-alert__body">
          <p>Every component page carries the same markup as a static fixture with a copy button,
          so you can take the snippets from there instead.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </noscript>

    <Section title="Snippet generator" num={1} lead={`Choose a component, a variant, a size and a theme for the panel. The markup is built from fixed templates and the HTML underneath is what you copy.`}>

    <form class="iv-grid iv-u-gap-4 iv-u-grid-cols-1 iv-u-md-grid-cols-3" id="pg-form" novalidate>
      <div class="iv-field">
        <label class="iv-label" for="pg-component">Component</label>
        <select class="iv-select" id="pg-component" name="component"></select>
      </div>
      <div class="iv-field">
        <label class="iv-label" for="pg-variant">Variant</label>
        <select class="iv-select" id="pg-variant" name="variant"></select>
      </div>
      <div class="iv-field" id="pg-size-field">
        <label class="iv-label" for="pg-size">Size</label>
        <select class="iv-select" id="pg-size" name="size"></select>
      </div>
      <div class="iv-field">
        <label class="iv-label" for="pg-text">Sample text</label>
        <select class="iv-select" id="pg-text" name="text"></select>
        <p class="iv-field__help iv-u-m-0" id="pg-text-help">Closed list: the playground never inserts text you type.</p>
      </div>
      <fieldset class="iv-fieldset">
        <legend class="iv-fieldset__legend">Preview theme</legend>
        <div class="iv-checks iv-checks--inline">
          <label class="iv-check"><input type="radio" name="pg-theme" value="light" checked> Light</label>
          <label class="iv-check"><input type="radio" name="pg-theme" value="dark"> Dark</label>
          <label class="iv-check"><input type="radio" name="pg-theme" value="system"> System</label>
        </div>
      </fieldset>
    </form>

    <figure class="docs-fixture" id="pg-fixture">
      <figcaption class="docs-fixture__caption">
        <span class="docs-fixture__title">Generated snippet</span>
        <span class="docs-fixture__path">playground</span>
        <button class="iv-button iv-button--secondary iv-button--sm docs-copy" type="button" data-copy-target="pg-code" aria-describedby="pg-status">Copy HTML</button>
        <span class="iv-u-sr-only" id="pg-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></span>
      </figcaption>
      <div class="docs-fixture__preview" id="pg-preview" data-iv-theme="light" role="group" aria-label="Live preview"></div>
      <div class="docs-fixture__code">
        <pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Generated HTML"><code id="pg-code"></code></pre>
      </div>
    </figure>

    <p class="iv-u-m-0"><a id="pg-doc-link" href="/components/button">Open the Button component page</a></p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="From snippet to page" num={2}>
      <p>The copied HTML works in any page that links the stylesheet and puts <code>class="iv-root"</code> on the <code>html</code> element. That is the whole setup:</p>
      <pre tabindex="0"><code>&lt;html class="iv-root" data-iv-theme="system"&gt;
  &lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="ivolt/css/ivolt.min.css"&gt;
  &lt;!-- paste the snippet here --&gt;
  &lt;script type="module" src="ivolt/js/auto.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;</code></pre>
      <p>The script line is only needed for components that come alive with JavaScript (the snippet carries a <code>data-iv-component</code> attribute when it does). Content components such as buttons, badges, alerts and cards are CSS only. The theme radio above only sets <code>data-iv-theme</code> on the preview panel; put the same attribute on any element of your page to theme that part of it.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Going further" num={3}>
      <ul>
        <li>Every component page has a live stage with the real file running, controls for theme, direction, width and motion, and the full markup.</li>
        <li>The <a href="/foundations/theme-builder">theme builder</a> changes the brand colours, radius and font and prints the CSS to paste after the stylesheet.</li>
        <li>The <a href="/examples">examples</a> are four complete pages built only with iVOLT, ready to download.</li>
        <li>The <a href="/reference">reference</a> lists every class, token, attribute and event, generated from the sources.</li>
      </ul>
    </Section>
  </article>

  <script src="../scripts/playground.js"></script>
</Base>
